  note    such an option takes its value only after `=` or joined to its short name, never from the next argument, as clap's `require_equals` reads it

capability flags/end-of-options  `--` ending the options, and options among the positionals
  heroes  flags.parse
  go      FlagSet.Parse
  rust    clap::Command::try_get_matches_from
  python  parse_args, parse_intermixed_args, parse_known_intermixed_args
  note    options and positionals stand in any order, as argparse, clap and GNU read them; Go stops at the first positional, which is `with_options_first`

capability flags/options-first  every argument from the first positional on taken as a positional, for a command that runs another
  heroes  flags.with_options_first
  go      FlagSet.Parse
  rust    clap::Command::trailing_var_arg, Arg::trailing_var_arg, Arg::last
